><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251014102935+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251014102937+10'00'" name="063ac9af-b0db-48c1-9037-560e6d3eb5bb" page="10" coords="54.482178,495.814758,293.547791,495.814758,54.482178,486.019470,293.547791,486.019470,42.519714,485.383362,293.541656,485.383362,42.519714,475.588074,293.541656,475.588074,42.519714,474.895386,293.539124,474.895386,42.519714,465.100098,293.539124,465.100098,42.519714,464.463989,293.597382,464.463989,42.519714,454.668701,293.597382,454.668701,42.519714,453.976013,293.548523,453.976013,42.519714,444.180725,293.548523,444.180725,42.519714,443.544617,293.543823,443.544617,42.519714,433.749329,293.543823,433.749329,42.519714,433.056641,293.545319,433.056641,42.519714,423.261353,293.545319,423.261353,42.519714,422.625244,293.567139,422.625244,42.519714,412.829956,293.567139,412.829956,42.519714,412.137268,293.552246,412.137268,42.519714,402.341980,293.552246,402.341980,42.519714,401.705872,293.549072,401.705872,42.519714,391.910583,293.549072,391.583923,42.519684,391.217896,293.599762,391.217896,42.519684,381.422607,293.599762,381.422607,42.519684,380.786499,293.614563,380.786499,42.519684,370.991211,293.614563,370.991211,42.519684,370.298523,293.514099,370.298523,42.519684,360.503235,293.514099,360.503235,42.519699,359.867126,293.484497,359.867126,42.519699,350.071838,293.484497,350.071838,42.519699,349.379150,293.532227,349.379150,42.519699,339.583862,293.532227,339.583862,42.519699,338.947754,293.560730,338.947754,42.519699,329.152466,293.560730,329.152466,42.519699,328.459778,293.508911,328.459778,42.519699,318.664490,293.508911,318.664490,42.519699,318.028381,293.567688,318.028381,42.519699,308.233093,293.567688,308.233093,42.519699,307.540405,293.544586,307.540405,42.519699,297.745117,293.544586,297.745117,42.519699,297.109009,293.502808,297.109009,42.519699,287.313721,293.502808,287.313721,42.519684,286.621033,293.562195,286.621033,42.519684,276.825745,293.562195,276.825745,42.519684,276.189636,293.506744,276.189636,42.519684,266.394348,293.506744,266.394348,42.519684,265.701660,79.097366,265.701660,42.519684,255.906372,79.097366,255.906372" rect="42.203400,255.600266,293.920654,496.120850" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This is the first paper to highlight the importance of solving the&#xD;problem of repairing fragmented tracks using a data driven approach.&#xD;Fragmented tracks often occur in the output of existing&#xD;multi-object tracking algorithms, particularly when there is object&#xD;occlusion. Our experiments showed that using the common solution&#xD;of linear interpolation to repair these fragmented tracks gives poor&#xD;performance for two real world team sports datasets. In contrast,&#xD;we propose a data driven approach for fragmented track repair that&#xD;uses a 1D CNNs encoder-decoder architecture. Our experiments&#xD;showed our 1D-CNN encoder-decoder based solutions significantly&#xD;outperforms linear interpolation in terms of Mean IOU of predicted&#xD;bounding boxes and the ground truth. Further, the experiments&#xD;show predicting the delta from linear interpolation significantly outperforms&#xD;directly outputting the bounding boxes in the untracked&#xD;gap. Our results also showed using 1D-CNN models for the encoder&#xD;and decoder produced better results than using GRU and 1D CNN&#xD;GRU hybrid. Finally we presented results demonstrating that our&#xD;proposed methods can improve the overall accuracy of the&#xD;Tracktor++ </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>[3] </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>and DeepSort </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>[33] </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>tracking algorithms. For future&#xD;work we want to design better re-identification algorithms for associating&#xD;left and right segments of the fragmented tracks and also improve&#xD;object detection performance during periods of object&#xD;occlusion.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="10" rect="595.276001,403.814758,779.276001,495.814758"
/></highlight
